From ea0e1a57c45ac3fb29eccb7458f3395c9e37e947 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: York Jasper Niebuhr <yjn@yjn-systems.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 15:57:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Added fieldlabel width constant definitions

This patch extends the fieldlabel feature to make GAS also define a
constant of the size of the labeled field.

An example for the extended fieldlabel feature is:

    movq $fieldlabel(42, .Lsome_label, .Lsome_width_label), %0

This causes GAS to put the .Lsome_label directly onto the bytes that
encode the immediate value 42. Additionally, GAS defines the
.Lsome_width_label as a constant that is the size of the immediate
field.

The fieldlabel test is expanded to also test if the width constants are
properly defined.

